 Unfortunately, the sata_sil driver of kernel 2.6.14 doesn't work on my
new Gigabyte K8N Ultra-9 m/b with the Sil3114 chip.. The disks are
generally detected (sometimes one of them not), but every disk I/O ends
up in "DriveStatusError" that later turns into "Command Timeout" and the
box locks up without any other message. The sata_nv prints weird
added/removed lines at the loading of the module, but that's works at
least.. If further info or testing needed just ask me


Gigabyte K8N Ultra-9 (bios version FC3)
Sil3114 BIOS: SoftRAID5 5.1.39
kernel 2.6.14
2x Maxtors on NV (sda, sdb)
2x Maxtors on Sil3114 (sdc, sdd)

I can reproduce it with:
 badblocks -sv /dev/sd[cd]
 badblocks -svw /dev/sd[cd]


full dmesg at http://scully.index.hu/dap/dmesg

